00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:04.730 align:start position:0%
after two years of negotiations we have  achieved a detailed arrangement that  permanently prohibits Iran from  obtaining a nuclear weapon it does not  resolve all problems certainly doesn't  resolve all our problems with Iran it  does not ensure a warming between our  two countries under this deal Iran  cannot acquire the plutonium needed for  a bomb Iran has powerful incentives to  keep its commitments if we're on  violates the agreement over the next  decade all of the sanctions can snap  back into place nuclear material isn't  something you hide in the closet it can  leave a trace for years the bottom line  is if Iran cheats we can catch them and  we will you are going to hear a lot of  arguments against this deal backed by  tens of millions of dollars in  advertising and if the rhetoric in these  ads and the accompanying commentary  sounds familiar it should for many of  the same people who argued for the war  in Iraq for now making the case against  the Iran nuclear deal ironically the  single greatest beneficiary in the  region of that war was the Islamic  Republic of Iran by killing this deal  Congress would not merely pave Iran's  pathway to a bomb it would accelerate it  those who say we can just walk away from  this deal and maintain sanctions are  selling a fantasy instead of  strengthening our position as some have  suggested Congress's rejection would  almost certainly result in multilateral  sanctions unraveling their opponents of  this deal who accept the choice of war  in fact they argue that surgical strikes  against Iran's facilities will be quick  and painless  but if we've learned anything from the  last decade it's that wars in general  and wars in the Middle East in  particular are anything but simple  Israel can defend itself against any  conventional danger whether from Iran  directly or from its proxies on the  other hand a nuclear-armed Iran changes  that equation there are times when force  is necessary and if Iran does not abide  by this deal it's possible that we don't  have an alternative but how can we in  good conscience justify war before we've  tested a diplomatic agreement that  achieves our objectives so this deal is  not just the best choice among  alternatives this is the strongest  non-proliferation agreement ever  negotiate
 

